# The axes this notebook explores.
#
# A chapter index tags itself with `categories:` drawn from this file, and rule
# 36 refuses anything that is not here. That is the whole drift protection:
# without it you get "5mm", "5 mm" and "5 mm foam" as three separate tags and the
# grouping quietly stops working.
#
# IT LIVES IN THE NOTEBOOK, not in `nb`, on purpose. An axis is something a
# notebook notices about ITSELF, usually after several chapters exist -- the
# chapter that first varies the foam thickness cannot know that thickness will
# become an axis. So adding a term is one line here, not a change to the tool,
# and retrofitting a new axis across the existing chapters is a frontmatter edit
# per chapter. Keep those edits cheap: nothing on a chapter index should execute.
#
# The axis names are for readers of this file. Rule 36 checks membership in the
# flattened set of values, so a term may sit under any axis.

axes:
  # What the aircraft is made of, or how big it is -- the vehicle itself.
  vehicle:
    - <a material, a size, a configuration>

  # How it was sized: by hand, by optimiser, by what objective.
  method:
    - <how the numbers were arrived at>

  # What the model includes and leaves out.
  fidelity:
    - <a component modelled, or a constraint imposed>
